          "id": "2",
          "prompt": "Who says “Güle güle!”?",
          "options": [
            "The one who stays",
            "The one who leaves",
            "Both at once"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Güle güle — “go smiling”: the one who stays says it. In English both people say “bye,” but in Turkish the one leaving says Hoşça kal."
        },
        {
          "id": "3",
          "prompt": "Which form comes from “okumak”?",
          "options": [
            "okuya okuya",
            "okua okua",
            "okuye okuye"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "oku ends in a vowel — we add y. The last vowel u is back, so it's -ya. English just adds “-ing”; Turkish needs y first."
        },
        {
          "id": "4",
          "prompt": "Sora sora buldum.",
          "say": "Sora sora buldum.",
          "options": [
